# Vertical slice = the game

## Non-negotiable truth

The **main-scene run** (today: scripts under `Prologue/`, `PrologueController`) is the **vertical slice** of Terraforming Tendencies—the same loop the **shipped game** will use: planet surface, sectors, survey-as-puzzle, typed resources, cards, placement, build weeks, End Week, corporate pressure.

**`Prologue` in a type or folder name is legacy organization from what shipped first—not a license to build a parallel “real game” later.**

## Do

- Extend **slice systems** toward the full product: `PrologueController`, `PrologueColony`, shared planet (`PlanetGenerator`, `SectorManager`), cards, `ColonyTileGrid`, placement, HUD.
- Frame plans as **game-wide** (perf, DOTS, culling, fog, economy, UI)—applicable as the slice grows (more sectors, planet pick), not “for prologue only.”
- Treat **player verification** on the slice as verifying **the game** ([`player-verify-after-changes.mdc`](player-verify-after-changes.mdc)).
- Use **archived** only where the repo already says so (e.g. **Colony Acts**), not for the vertical slice.

## Do not

- Call the slice a **separate module**, **tutorial**, **demo**, **one-off**, or **side quest**.
- Propose **prologue-only** code paths, **prologue-only** optimizations, or **“defer until full game”** for core mechanics.
- Split architecture into “prologue” vs “real game” (e.g. two fog systems, two economies) without explicit user direction.
- Dismiss folder names (`Prologue*`) as “not production” when they **own the authoritative run** today.

## Quick reference

| | |
|--|--|
| **Authoritative run** | Vertical slice / `PrologueController` path |
| **Archived** | Colony Acts (`ColonyActManager` must not own run when slice active) |
| **Agent router** | [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) — default: PK **§0** + **§2** only |

When unsure, read the router + §0 before changing architecture.

## How agents talk to the player (required)

The player is building **Terraforming Tendencies**, not a side “prologue project.”

**Use when explaining work:** the **game**, **main run**, **vertical slice**, **current run**, **main scene**, **slice systems**.

**Do not use as the framing** (especially in summaries, plans, and “what I did”): “prologue work”, “prologue feature”, “prologue UX”, “for the prologue”, “prologue-only task”, “the prologue game”, “finishing the prologue”.

**OK when precise:** citing paths or types (`PrologueController`, `Assets/Scripts/Prologue/`, step 0–6) — then say they are **legacy folder/type names** for the **authoritative run**, not a separate product.

**New naming:** do not add new top-level `Prologue*` types, scenes, or docs that imply a fork unless the user asks. Extend existing shared systems (`CardDeckController`, `PlanetGenerator`, `SectorManager`, HUD, colony sim).

**Harness/script names** (`prologue-ui-playthrough.sh`, etc.) are historical filenames; describe them as **game / slice playtests**, not “prologue tests”.